  "claim": "Deflated Sharpe ratio (Bailey and Lopez de Prado 2014) and CSCV probability of backtest overfitting (Bailey, Borwein, Lopez de Prado and Zhu 2017) were computed offline over the 6605-record research-evaluation candidate ledger (301 aligned development episodes, 2015-01-02 to 2020-12-16). For the frozen four-candidate selection set the highest-Sharpe candidate (momentum120, per-episode Sharpe 0.0254) has DSR 0.5521 against SR0 0.0177, and PBO is 0.7756 (S=16, mean-label metric, 12870 combinations). The walk-forward selected series has Sharpe -0.0151 and PSR(0) 0.4048. The retained candidates show no deflated-Sharpe evidence of skill, and the in-sample best candidate usually ranks below the out-of-sample median.",
