  "conclusion": [
    "DSR of the best retained selection candidate is 0.552 (momentum120), far below a 0.95 confidence threshold, even though only four trials are deflated; its undeflated PSR(0) is 0.667. Adding the equal-weight control (best: equalweight, DSR 0.575) or restricting to momentum rules (DSR 0.561) does not change this.",
    "PBO is 0.776 for the primary set (S=16, mean label): the in-sample best candidate ranks below the out-of-sample median in about three of four CSCV splits (N=4, so no split lands exactly on the median). Every sensitivity cell (S 8 to 16, mean or Sharpe metric, three trial sets) has PBO (lambda <= 0) between 0.76 and 0.96; the strict lambda < 0 share is lower where an odd trial count allows exact median ties (momentum-only N=3: 0.34 to 0.48; with the control N=5: 0.62 to 0.76). The retained degradation_slope values (primary -0.727) are not used as evidence: with the mean metric and equal complementary halves, a trial's in-sample plus out-of-sample mean equals twice its mean over the used rows, so splits selecting the same trial lie on a slope of exactly -1 (momentum120 is selected in 5490 of 12870 splits).",
    "The frozen walk-forward selector's development out-of-sample series (249 episodes over 20 folds) has negative mean and Sharpe -0.0151, PSR(0) 0.405. This is consistent with the research-evaluation README, which makes no persistent-advantage claim for the training-selected rule.",
    "Conclusion: over these retained candidates the evidence is consistent with selection noise, not skill. The no-skill PBO for four exchangeable trials is about 0.5, so a PBO of 0.776 is also consistent with mild anti-persistence of in-sample ranking; the CSCV splits overlap heavily and PBO carries no p-value, so this reading is descriptive. This is a negative diagnostic for this three-ETF control lane; it neither tunes, promotes nor rejects any future strategy."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Inputs are raw-price five-session labels less a fixed 20bp proxy, not portfolio returns; the Sharpe ratios are per-episode label ratios, not investable or annualized Sharpe ratios.",
    "The trial count is only this lane's frozen candidate set (4, sensitivity 3 and 5). Trials run elsewhere in the research program are not counted, so the DSR here is an optimistic upper bound relative to program-wide multiple testing; no effective-N clustering was applied although momentum60 and momentum120 share 60% of development labels.",
